=== INVENTORY (implementation step 1) — gaps found ===
================================================================================
The 226 P7 surfaces were generated and individually verified in ISOLATION
(per-surface SwiftPM build), but NEVER co-compiled into the app/test modules.
Compiling them together surfaced the integration debt this gate had to clear:

  1. CO-LOCATED TESTS MIS-WIRED. 261 *Tests.swift / *.ModelTests.swift /
     *.AdapterTests.swift / *.ViewTests.swift / *.StateTests.swift lived under
     the APP target's source roots (they `import XCTest` + `@testable import
     TeslaSync`), so the app target failed to build. → project.yml now excludes
     `*Tests.swift` from TeslaSync / TeslaSync-macOS and includes them in
     TeslaSyncTests / TeslaSync-macOSTests.
  2. 109 cross-surface top-level TYPE-NAME COLLISIONS (e.g. RecentDrives*,
     VehicleHero*, TelemetryErrors*, ChargerType*, DashboardWidgetSize/
     Registration, Drivetrain*, JSONValue) — independent surfaces declaring the
     same module-scope type. Cascaded into 1260 compile errors (incl. an
     @Observable-macro key-path storm from a duplicate `TelemetryErrorsModel`).
  3. 23 duplicate XCTestCase class names + 1 private/internal test-double clash
     across co-located test files.
  4. Pre-existing P7 source defects that only fail when co-compiled under Swift 6
     strict concurrency / one module: custom `Stepper` shadowing SwiftUI.Stepper;
     nonisolated preview helpers calling @MainActor models; `static let`
     DateFormatter/closures not Sendable; @MainActor `resolvePhase`/`surfaceSlug`
     read from nonisolated tests; non-`@escaping` ForEach closure; macOS-only
     `onExitCommand` unguarded; a type-check-timeout expression; 3 test files
     missing `@testable import TeslaSync`; 8 wrong test expectations/fixtures.

Existing infra suites (P1..P8, all green here): Facade/golden (UnitsGoldenVector
